## Part 2: Mathematical Formulas Reference## Linear System Formulas (State Recovery)
When the developer uses a standard Linear Congruential Generator (LCG):

   1. The State Formula:
   $$X_{n+1} = (a \cdot X_n + c) \pmod m$$ 
   2. The Multiplier Discovery Formula:
   $$a \equiv (X_3 - X_2) \cdot (X_2 - X_1)^{-1} \pmod m$$ 
   3. The Inverse Discovery Formula (Extended Euclidean Algorithm): Find an integer $y$ such that:
   $$(X_2 - X_1) \cdot y \equiv 1 \pmod m \quad \text{where } y = (X_2 - X_1)^{-1}$$ 

## Non-Linear System Formulas (Statistical Edge Discovery)
When the system uses a secure generator (like ChaCha20) but introduces modulo bias via bad mapping math (value % 360):

   1. Expected Frequency ($E_i$):
   $$E_i = \frac{N}{k}$$ 
   (Where $N$ = total collected spins, $k$ = total wheel slices)
   2. Chi-Square Goodness-of-Fit Test ($\chi^2$):
   $$\chi^2 = \sum_{i=1}^{k} \frac{(O_i - E_i)^2}{E_i}$$ 
   (Where $O_i$ = the actual observed count for slice $i$)

